    "Notes Updated": "12/15/2024",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter?\n Great pitcher's frame, but the velo hasn't really jumped much as a starter, still usually 89 92 T94. We've seen it sit more in the 91 94 T96 range as a reliever.\n Doesn't walk many batters but strikeouts are down from where they were a couple years ago\n Uses his fastball to get the job done. Doesn't have premiere velocity, it has a really good shape with plus spin and IVB. \n His slider is now a mid 70's offering with more sweep than sharp movement.\n Changeup is the best pitch for me right now but still an average offering in the mid 80's.\n Still throwing his loopy curveball in the upper 60's and low 70's.\n Without the velo jump as a starter, not sure there's a ton here anymore, unfortunately.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/19/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Starter?\n  Great pitcher's frame, but a lot of room to project more weight to be added. \n  Throws with some effort, but uses his lower half well. \n  High 3/4 arm slot.\n  Doesn't walk many batters and has been striking out a ton. \n  Uses his fastball to get the job done. Doesn't have premiere velocity, it has a really good shape with plus spin and IVB. \n  Also has good slider and feel for changeup. \n  Average spin on the slider.\n  He also throws a curveball that is a much slower velo than his other pitches. Flashes being decent but isn't great presently. \n  If everything clicks, this is the kind of arm that the Brewers do well with and can turn into a rotation piece.",
